Commands

docker ps
(shows current containers)

docker build .
(builds the image from the Dockerfile in the current directory)

docker stop container-name
(stops the container with the specified name)

docker run -p hostPort:containerPort image-name
(runs the image with port mapping from host to container)

docker start container-name
(starts a container, does not show the logs) (unatached) (detach)

docker attach container-name
(show logs from a container in terminal)

docker rm container-names
(removes containers)

docker images
(lists images)

docker rmi
(removes images)

docker image prune
(removes unused images)

docker cp file/files container-name:/directory
(copy a local file to a container directory)

docker cp container-name:/directory file/files
(copy a container file to a local directory)

docker ....... -v volumeName:containerLocation
(links the folder in the container to the volume, creates the volume if needed). Named volumes are no deleted on container shut down

Ex:
docker run -p 3000:80 -d --name feedback-app -v feedbackS3:/app/feedback --rm feedback:latest

Ex 2:
docker run -p 3000:80 -d --name feedback-app -v feedbackS3:/app/feedback -v absolute-path-to-src:/app --rm feedback:latest
(keeps the source code in a volume so it updates automatically)

When you have multiple volumes in a container the longest path volume will not be overwritten if you overwrite another folder for example

docker run -d -p 3000:80 --name feedback-app -v feedback:/app/feedback -v "/Users/maximilianschwarzmuller/development/teaching/udemy/docker-complete:/app" -v /app/node_modules feedback-node:volumes

